---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="home-title">
    <h1 id="home-title">John Company: Second Edition</h1>
    <p>
      An unofficial browser edition of Cole Wehrle's game. Play at one table, or take your turns
      and pass the save file to whoever acts next.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/play/">Play</a>
      <a class="button" href="/online/">Play online</a>
      <a class="button" href="/how-to-play/">How to play</a>
      <a class="button" href="/rules/">Rules</a>
      <a class="button" href="/credits/">Credits</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <h2>What works today</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>1710</strong> (5 turns), <strong>1758</strong> (Company Under Siege, turns 3 to 7),
      <strong>1813</strong> (Post Monopoly, turns 5 to 8, best with 5 or 6 players) and
      <strong>Long 1710</strong> (8 turns, with the Vote to Deregulate and private firms), for 3 to 6 players, with every phase played by the rules, or alone or with one friend against the Crown (from a save file, not online), in any scenario.
    </li>
    <li>
      Play at one table, pass a save file to whoever acts next, or <a href="/online/">play online</a>
      with a private link for each player.
    </li>
    <li>Undo, the full rules reference, and a log of every roll.</li>
  </ul>
</SiteLayout>
